<dl>
    <dt>Account</dt>
    <dd>An access to the site, with an e-mail address, a password and a language.</dd>
    <dt>Extension</dt>
    <dd>A folder that adds a feature to the core - a kind of catalogue, for example. Only one is active at a time.</dd>
    <dt>Feature (of an extension)</dt>
    <dd>Something a plan can unlock. What a feature actually does is decided by the relevant extension.</dd>
    <dt>Invoice</dt>
    <dd>The record of a subscription payment, numbered in sequence, with VAT taken out of it.</dd>
    <dt>Category</dt>
    <dd>A point in the tree that offers are filed under.</dd>
    <dt>Module</dt>
    <dd>A built-in function of the core that can be switched off, for example reviews or subscriptions. Off means: no routes, no menu entry, the data stays.</dd>
    <dt>Offer</dt>
    <dd>What a provider lists in the catalogue: a service, an auction lot and the like, depending on the active extension.</dd>
    <dt>Order</dt>
    <dd>The purchase of an offer, with its history, messages and payment.</dd>
    <dt>Package</dt>
    <dd>The delivery of an extension or a theme as a downloadable zip file, through a repository or by upload.</dd>
    <dt>Permission</dt>
    <dd>A single allowance to do something in the administration. Permissions are granted through roles.</dd>
    <dt>Plan</dt>
    <dd>A subscription offer with a price, a period, and the features it includes.</dd>
    <dt>Provider</dt>
    <dd>An account with its own, approved profile that may list offers.</dd>
    <dt>Role</dt>
    <dd>A set of permissions assigned to an account.</dd>
    <dt>Subscription</dt>
    <dd>A plan the operator sells directly - independent of the marketplace. See the chapter "Subscriptions".</dd>
    <dt>Theme</dt>
    <dd>A folder that decides what the public site looks like. Only one is active at a time.</dd>
    <dt>Webhook</dt>
    <dd>A notification a payment service (Stripe, for example) sends to the site on its own, such as when a subscription has been renewed.</dd>
    <dt>Withdrawal</dt>
    <dd>A buyer's declaration that they are backing out of an order.</dd>
</dl>
